WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.735
-This is a very famous photo,
and I wanted to bring it out,

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I --
It just is so lovely,

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:06.506 size:81% position:41%
you know, how much fun
you guys are having.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.174 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.710
And what was -- You know,
what was it like working with --

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again, 'cause it was
the beginning for all of you.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.581
What was it like working
with young Harrison Ford?

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.583
-Oh, my gosh.
Well, the thing is, he walked --

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:19.919
George likes to cast people that
are so close to what he wants,

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
he doesn't have
to really get in there

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
and give you
a lot of directions.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:23.456 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:26.092
-So, Harrison walks in, and he's
just too cool for school.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:26.693 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I just --
Instant idolization.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:32.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, Carrie was funny
and witty and adorable.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:37.337 size:84% position:42%
And we just -- we just
immediately hit it off.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:38.671 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was perfect.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:42.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Harrison had a really firm
grasp, like the overview.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:46.746
I think he'd make a really good
director if he weren't so lazy.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.416 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.084 line:92%
We'll edit that out later.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:51.951 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:56.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
But for instance,
we were doing a scene where --

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:59.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was right after we got out
of the trash compactor.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:00:59.926 line:92%
We hadn't filmed that scene yet.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:02.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm looking in continuity,
and I said, "Wait a second.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:05.498
This is right after we got
out of the trash compactor.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
Shouldn't my hair
be all wet and matted

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.102 line:92%
with schmutz all through it?"

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he turns to me,
and he says...

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:14.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Deep voice ] "Hey, kid,
it ain't that kind of movie."

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:19.312 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:23.416
"If people are looking at your
hair, we're all in big trouble."

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.717 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ]
And I thought, "He's so..."

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:30.123 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
"He's so right."
-He's so right.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And next time I saw him,
he said,

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:36.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Deep voice ]
"Hey, I don't sound
anything like that."

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.498 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ]
But, like I say, I mean,

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:42.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
you'd have these moments
of self-awareness

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you're standing in
the cockpit waiting between --

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause once the squibs go off,
you have to stand up there.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.175
"Kids, if you can stay up
instead of coming down,

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:51.111 size:78% position:39%
they're gonna rewire
and do another take."

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'd have this moment
of self-awareness.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:56.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
To my right is one of
the most venerated actors

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.451 size:75% position:38%
of the 20th century,
Sir Alec Guinness.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-To my left is an 8-foot guy

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a dog costume,
wearing headphones.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.791 line:92%
-What's wrong with this picture?

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:07.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, the crazy thing now is,
obviously, you know,

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.729
it's part of, you know,
our lexicon to say things

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:10.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
like "lightsaber"
and "Death Star."

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, right, right.
-But when you read the script,

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:13.333 line:92%
did it all seem so absurd

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.502
before we knew
what it was going to look like?

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:20.573
-Well, what's amazing to me
is that I was just overwhelmed.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.610
'Cause I got the part
without having read the script.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.944 line:92%
I just did a screen test.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I didn't know
what the style was

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:30.483
or whether it's a send-up
like Mel Brooks or what.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then when I read it,
it just hit me.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:34.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "This is more like
'Wizard of Oz'

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:36.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
than traditional
science fiction.'"

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:40.393 size:88% position:44%
'Cause, I mean, "2001"
is a stone-cold classic.

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:42.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
A laugh riot it ain't.
-Right.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:45.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this one was so funny.
-Yeah.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:46.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean,
it was so on a human level.

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:50.703
I mean, we risk our lives
to rescue the princess.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
She takes a look
at what we came in

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.607 line:92%
and said, "You came in that?"

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
who says things like that?

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:56.943 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And robots arguing
over whose fault it is.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
I knew I was the straight man.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.517 size:88% position:44%
though, "Ooh, every part
is funnier than mine."

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:08.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
if you appreciate comedy,

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:12.759
you realize what Bud Abbott
is doing for Lou Costello.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:14.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know, so, you know,

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you say Threepio,
"That little friend of yours

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
is gonna get me
in a lot of trouble."

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.800 line:92%
"Oh, he excels at that, sir."

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you're
lining it up for me,

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.304 line:92%
then knock it out of the park.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:26.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
But leave it to George Lucas
to write a script

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:29.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
where the robots
get better lines than me.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.243 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:33.813
-Well, in the long run, I think
it worked out for everybody.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, no,
listen, I couldn't be happier.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's very surreal
to have you here.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
I spent a lot of time
in my youth watching you,

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.089
and it is just -- what a joy it
is to have you here right now.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:45.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, in your adulthood,
you should watch "Knightfall,"

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:49.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mondays, 10:00 p.m.
on History Channel.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.497 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:52.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I mean...

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:54.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause you know what happens?
You know what happens?

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
We go on these shows,
and I get sidetracked...

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...talking about Wookiees

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:02.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
and laser swords,
and I come off, I go,

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:04.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Ooh! I didn't even
mention 'Knightfall.'"

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, there you go --
"Knightfall,"

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:09.115 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Monday nights, History!

